From: ViKing <viking.yfy@qq.com>
Date: Sat, 14 Nov 2026 19:48:39 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: qcom: ipq9574: connect USB PIPE clock to GCC

The GCC binding and driver describe the USB3 PHY PIPE clock as the eighth
input, but the SoC DTS leaves it disconnected. The driver only looks up
this parent by its DT index, so usb0_pipe_clk_src remains an orphan even
when the QMP PHY has registered usb0_pipe_clk.

Connect the QMP PHY clock provider in the common SoC description, as is
already done for the PCIe PIPE inputs.

Signed-off-by: ViKing <viking.yfy@qq.com>

--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/ipq9574.dtsi
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/ipq9574.dtsi
@@ -452,7 +452,7 @@
 				 <&pcie1_phy>,
 				 <&pcie2_phy>,
 				 <&pcie3_phy>,
-				 <0>;
+				 <&usb_0_qmpphy>;
 			#clock-cells = <1>;
 			#reset-cells = <1>;
 			#interconnect-cells = <1>;
